KanaKSUCore - Credits & Attribution
====================================

KanaKSUCore is a minimal KernelSU core driver implemented for the SuiKernel
Vanilla build variant to provide native SELinux rule hooking (via Android
Vendor Hook tracepoints) and secondary manager tracking without requiring
the full standalone KernelSU module.

Most of KanaKSUCore's subsystem architecture, manager identity verification,
and hook patterns are referenced, adapted, and derived from:

1. KernelSU
   - Original Creator: weishu <tiann@tiann.net>
   - Contributors: KernelSU Team and contributors
   - Repository: https://github.com/tiann/KernelSU
   - License: GNU General Public License v3.0 (GPL-3.0)
   - Referenced Components:
     * manager/apk_sign.c, apk_sign.h (APK v2/v3 signature parsing and manager identification)
     * manager/throne_tracker.c, throne_tracker.h (Manager tracking and UID registration)
     * include/ (Internal types, uapi, and helper macros)

2. KernelSU Next
   - Maintainers: KernelSU Next Team / rifsxd
   - Repository: https://github.com/KernelSU-Next/KernelSU-Next
   - License: GNU General Public License v3.0 (GPL-3.0)
   - Referenced Components:
     * Extended manager registration and hook abstractions
     * SELinux dynamic rule hooking via tracepoints/vendor hooks

3. SuiKernel Integration
   - Integrated, adapted, and maintained by: Kana Wesley Yamada
   - Tailored specifically for SuiKernel GKI builds and SuiKernel Manager integration.
